This project is a focused re-implementation of the server-side Hysteria2 and
AnyTLS protocols from the "shoes" project (https://github.com/cfal/shoes),
which is distributed under the MIT license.

The protocol logic (AnyTLS framing/multiplexing/padding, Hysteria2 HTTP/3 auth,
UDP relay and stream handling) is ported from and inspired by shoes' current
implementation (https://github.com/cfal/shoes), Copyright (c) 2025 cfal.

This project removes the proxy-chaining/rules engine and other protocols, and
forwards traffic directly to the requested destination.

